% ---------------------------------------------------------------------------
% What the model covers: the articles of the chapter's families, and made
% up textile articles.
% ---------------------------------------------------------------------------

% the model covers the made up articles, sets, worn articles and rags of
% Chapter 63
rule textile_articles_scope_family:
a good is a good the model describes
    if the family of the good is a family
    and the family is a family of chapter sixty-three goods.

% the model covers a made up textile article that names no kind (heading
% 6307 below)
rule textile_articles_scope_made_up:
a good is a good the model describes
    if the good is a made up textile article
    and it is not the case that
        the family of the good is a family.

blanket is a family of chapter sixty-three goods, as stated in HTSUS Chapter 63, confer "Blankets and traveling rugs:".
bed linen is a family of chapter sixty-three goods, as stated in HTSUS Chapter 63, confer "Bed linen, table linen, toilet linen and kitchen linen:".
table linen is a family of chapter sixty-three goods, as stated in HTSUS Chapter 63, confer "Bed linen, table linen, toilet linen and kitchen linen:".
toilet linen is a family of chapter sixty-three goods, as stated in HTSUS Chapter 63, confer "Bed linen, table linen, toilet linen and kitchen linen:".
kitchen linen is a family of chapter sixty-three goods, as stated in HTSUS Chapter 63, confer "Bed linen, table linen, toilet linen and kitchen linen:".
curtain is a family of chapter sixty-three goods, as stated in HTSUS Chapter 63, confer "Curtains (including drapes) and interior blinds; curtain or bed".
bedspread is a family of chapter sixty-three goods, as stated in HTSUS Chapter 63, confer "Bedspreads:".
bed net is a family of chapter sixty-three goods, as stated in HTSUS Chapter 63, confer "Bed nets specified in subheading note 1 to this chapter".
furnishing article is a family of chapter sixty-three goods, as stated in HTSUS Chapter 63, confer "Other furnishing articles, excluding those of heading 9404:".
packing sack is a family of chapter sixty-three goods, as stated in HTSUS Chapter 63, confer "Sacks and bags, of a kind used for the packing of goods:".
tarpaulin is a family of chapter sixty-three goods, as stated in HTSUS Chapter 63, confer "Tarpaulins, awnings and sunblinds:".
tent is a family of chapter sixty-three goods, as stated in HTSUS Chapter 63, confer "Tents (including temporary canopies and similar articles):".
sail is a family of chapter sixty-three goods, as stated in HTSUS Chapter 63, confer "sails for boats, sailboards or".
pneumatic mattress is a family of chapter sixty-three goods, as stated in HTSUS Chapter 63, confer "Pneumatic mattresses:".
camping goods is a family of chapter sixty-three goods, as stated in HTSUS Chapter 63, confer "landcraft; camping goods:".
cleaning cloth is a family of chapter sixty-three goods, as stated in HTSUS Chapter 63, confer "Floorcloths, dishcloths, dusters and similar cleaning cloths:".
lifejacket is a family of chapter sixty-three goods, as stated in HTSUS Chapter 63, confer "Lifejackets and lifebelts".
other made up article is a family of chapter sixty-three goods, as stated in HTSUS Chapter 63, confer "Other made up articles, including dress patterns:".
needlecraft set is a family of chapter sixty-three goods, as stated in HTSUS Chapter 63, confer "II. NEEDLECRAFT SETS".
rag is a family of chapter sixty-three goods, as stated in HTSUS Chapter 63, confer "Used or new rags, scrap twine, cordage, rope and cables".

% the families of subchapter I (made up articles, note 1)
rule subchapter_one_family with provenance HTSUS Chapter 63, confer "I. OTHER MADE UP TEXTILE ARTICLES":
a family is a family of subchapter one
    if the family is a family of chapter sixty-three goods
    and it is not the case that
        the family is in [needlecraft set, rag].

% The kinds of articles: the tariff's own words, and the rulings'
blanket falls in the family blanket, as stated in HTSUS Chapter 63, confer "Blankets and traveling rugs:".
traveling rug falls in the family blanket, as stated in HTSUS Chapter 63, confer "Blankets and traveling rugs:".
electric blanket falls in the family blanket, as stated in HTSUS Chapter 63, confer "Electric blankets (666)".
throw falls in the family blanket, as stated in ruling NY E80466, confer "The subject merchandise, referred to as a textile throw, is considered a blanket".
bed sheet falls in the family bed linen, as stated in HTSUS Chapter 63, confer "Sheets (361)".
flat sheet falls in the family bed linen, as stated in ruling NY N223636, confer "The set consists of a flat sheet, fitted sheet and two pillowcases".
fitted sheet falls in the family bed linen, as stated in ruling NY N223636, confer "The set consists of a flat sheet, fitted sheet and two pillowcases".
pillowcase falls in the family bed linen, as stated in HTSUS Chapter 63, confer "Pillowcases, other than bolster cases".
bolster case falls in the family bed linen, as stated in HTSUS Chapter 63, confer "Bolster cases (360)".
tablecloth falls in the family table linen, as stated in HTSUS Chapter 63, confer "Tablecloths and napkins:".
napkin falls in the family table linen, as stated in HTSUS Chapter 63, confer "Tablecloths and napkins:".
placemat falls in the family table linen, as stated in ruling NY N323770, confer "Item #895 is a placemat comprised of two layers of 100 percent polyester woven fabric".
towel falls in the family toilet linen, as stated in HTSUS Chapter 63, confer "Towels:".
bath towel falls in the family toilet linen, as stated in ruling NY N275351, confer "The set consists of a bath towel, hand towel, and washcloth".
hand towel falls in the family toilet linen, as stated in ruling NY N275351, confer "The set consists of a bath towel, hand towel, and washcloth".
