rag falls in the family rag, as stated in HTSUS Chapter 63, confer "Used or new rags, scrap twine, cordage, rope and cables".
scrap twine falls in the family rag, as stated in HTSUS Chapter 63, confer "Used or new rags, scrap twine, cordage, rope and cables".

% ---------------------------------------------------------------------------
% Made up articles of a textile fabric (Chapter 63 note 1; Section XI note
% 7).
% ---------------------------------------------------------------------------

% Section XI note 7: the ways that make an article "made up"
cutting otherwise than into squares or rectangles is a process of section eleven note seven,
    as stated in HTSUS Section XI and Chapter 50, confer "(a) Cut otherwise than into squares or rectangles;".
production in the finished state is a process of section eleven note seven,
    as stated in HTSUS Section XI and Chapter 50, confer "(b) Produced in the finished state, ready for use".
heat-sealing is a process of section eleven note seven,
    as stated in HTSUS Section XI and Chapter 50, confer "Cut to size and with at least one heat-sealed edge with a visibly tapered or compressed border".
hemming is a process of section eleven note seven,
    as stated in HTSUS Section XI and Chapter 50, confer "(d) Hemmed or with rolled edges, or with a knotted fringe at any of the edges".
drawn thread work is a process of section eleven note seven,
    as stated in HTSUS Section XI and Chapter 50, confer "(e) Cut to size and having undergone a process of drawn thread work;".
sewing is a process of section eleven note seven,
    as stated in HTSUS Section XI and Chapter 50, confer "(f) Assembled by sewing, gumming or otherwise".
gumming is a process of section eleven note seven,
    as stated in HTSUS Section XI and Chapter 50, confer "(f) Assembled by sewing, gumming or otherwise".
knitting to shape is a process of section eleven note seven,
    as stated in HTSUS Section XI and Chapter 50, confer "(g) Knitted or crocheted to shape".

% A finished article of a kind that subchapter I names (a blanket, a towel,
% a curtain...) is made up too: the subchapter names these articles "made
% up", and a listing offers a finished product.
rule note_xi_7 with provenance HTSUS Section XI and Chapter 50,
        confer "For the purposes of this section, the expression \"made up\" means:":
a good is made up
    if the good is made up by a process
        and the process is a process of section eleven note seven
    otherwise the good is a manufactured article
        and the family of the good is a family
        and the family is a family of subchapter one.

% of a textile fabric: a fabric construction, a textile material that the
% composition gives, or the text's word that the good is of textile
rule note_63_1_fabric with provenance HTSUS Chapter 63,
        confer "Subchapter 1 applies only to made up articles, of any textile fabric.":
a good is of textile fabric
    if the fabric construction of the good is a construction
    otherwise the good is of textile material
    otherwise the textile material of the good is a group.

% the good, or what it is classified as consisting of (GRI 3(b)), is made
% up and of a textile fabric
rule note_63_1 with provenance HTSUS Chapter 63,
        confer "Subchapter 1 applies only to made up articles, of any textile fabric.":
a good is a made up textile article
    if the good is made up
    and the good is classified as consisting of the good
    and the good is of textile fabric.

rule note_63_1_component with provenance HTSUS Chapter 63,
        confer "Subchapter 1 applies only to made up articles, of any textile fabric.":
a good is a made up textile article
    if a component is a component of the good
    and the good is classified as consisting of the component
    and the component is made up
    and the component is of textile fabric.

% ---------------------------------------------------------------------------
% The headings (GRI 1), each with the notes that take goods out of it.
% ---------------------------------------------------------------------------

rule heading_6301 with provenance HTSUS Chapter 63, confer "Blankets and traveling rugs:":
a good is described by heading 6301
    if the family of the good is blanket
    and the good is a made up textile article.

rule heading_6302 with provenance HTSUS Chapter 63,
        confer "Bed linen, table linen, toilet linen and kitchen linen:":
a good is described by heading 6302
    if the family of the good is a family
    and the family is in [bed linen, table linen, toilet linen, kitchen linen]
    and the good is a made up textile article.

rule heading_6303 with provenance HTSUS Chapter 63,
        confer "Curtains (including drapes) and interior blinds; curtain or bed":
a good is described by heading 6303
    if the family of the good is curtain
    and the good is a made up textile article.

rule heading_6304 with provenance HTSUS Chapter 63,
        confer "Other furnishing articles, excluding those of heading 9404:":
a good is described by heading 6304
    if the family of the good is a family
    and the family is in [bedspread, bed net, furnishing article]
    and the good is a made up textile article.

rule heading_6305 with provenance HTSUS Chapter 63,
        confer "Sacks and bags, of a kind used for the packing of goods:":
a good is described by heading 6305
    if the family of the good is packing sack
    and the good is a made up textile article.

% a bag that names no kind of the chapter, of a kind used for packing: the
% principal use is a judgment of the office (HTSUS Additional U.S. Rule of
% Interpretation 1(a), chapter_39.le)
rule heading_6305_use with provenance HTSUS Chapter 63,
        confer "Sacks and bags, of a kind used for the packing of goods:":
a good is described by heading 6305
    if the good is a made up textile article
    and the principal use of the good is packing of goods
    and it is not the case that
        the family of the good is a family.

rule heading_6306 with provenance HTSUS Chapter 63,
        confer "Tarpaulins, awnings and sunblinds; tents (including temporary":
a good is described by heading 6306
    if the family of the good is a family
    and the family is in [tarpaulin, tent, sail, pneumatic mattress, camping goods]
    and the good is a made up textile article.

rule heading_6307 with provenance HTSUS Chapter 63,
        confer "Other made up articles, including dress patterns:":
a good is described by heading 6307
    if the family of the good is a family
    and the family is in [cleaning cloth, lifejacket, other made up article]
    and the good is a made up textile article.

% the residual heading: a made up textile article that names no kind (a
% kind that the model does not list leaves the good unplaced)
rule heading_6307_other with provenance HTSUS Chapter 63,
        confer "Other made up articles, including dress patterns:":
a good is described by heading 6307
    if the good is a made up textile article
    and it is not the case that
        the kind of the good is a kind
    and it is not the case that
        the family of the good is a family.

rule heading_6308 with provenance HTSUS Chapter 63,
        confer "Needlecraft sets consisting of woven fabric and yarn, whether":
a good is described by heading 6308
    if the family of the good is needlecraft set
    and the good is put up in packings for retail sale.

% Note 3: heading 6309 takes only the articles the note lists, with signs
% of appreciable wear, entered in bulk or in bales, sacks or similar
% packings
rule heading_6309 with provenance HTSUS Chapter 63,
        confer "Heading 6309 applies only to the following goods:":
a good is described by heading 6309
    if the good is an article of chapter sixty-three note three
    and the good shows signs of appreciable wear
    and the good is entered in bulk or in bales, sacks or similar packings.

rule note_63_3a_clothing with provenance HTSUS Chapter 63,
        confer "Clothing and clothing accessories, and parts thereof;":
a good is an article of chapter sixty-three note three
    if the good is a garment
    or the good is a clothing accessory.

rule note_63_3a_textiles with provenance HTSUS Chapter 63, confer "Articles of textile materials:":
a good is an article of chapter sixty-three note three
    if the family of the good is a family
    and the family is a family of the textile articles of note three
    and the good is of textile fabric.

% (b) footwear of any material other than asbestos (headgear of Chapter 65
% is not modelled)
rule note_63_3b with provenance HTSUS Chapter 63,
        confer "Footwear and headgear of any material other than asbestos.":
a good is an article of chapter sixty-three note three
    if the family of the good is footwear.

blanket is a family of the textile articles of note three, as stated in HTSUS Chapter 63, confer "Blankets and traveling rugs;".
bed linen is a family of the textile articles of note three, as stated in HTSUS Chapter 63, confer "Bed linen, table linen, toilet linen and kitchen linen;".
table linen is a family of the textile articles of note three, as stated in HTSUS Chapter 63, confer "Bed linen, table linen, toilet linen and kitchen linen;".
toilet linen is a family of the textile articles of note three, as stated in HTSUS Chapter 63, confer "Bed linen, table linen, toilet linen and kitchen linen;".
kitchen linen is a family of the textile articles of note three, as stated in HTSUS Chapter 63, confer "Bed linen, table linen, toilet linen and kitchen linen;".
curtain is a family of the textile articles of note three, as stated in HTSUS Chapter 63, confer "Furnishings, other than carpets of headings 5701 to 5705 and tapestries of heading 5805.".
bedspread is a family of the textile articles of note three, as stated in HTSUS Chapter 63, confer "Furnishings, other than carpets of headings 5701 to 5705 and tapestries of heading 5805.".
furnishing article is a family of the textile articles of note three, as stated in HTSUS Chapter 63, confer "Furnishings, other than carpets of headings 5701 to 5705 and tapestries of heading 5805.".

rule heading_6310 with provenance HTSUS Chapter 63,
        confer "Used or new rags, scrap twine, cordage, rope and cables, and":
a good is described by heading 6310
    if the family of the good is rag.

% Note 2(a): goods of Chapters 56 to 62 are not of subchapter I (here, the
% garments and clothing accessories of Chapters 61 and 62)
rule note_63_2a with provenance HTSUS Chapter 63, confer "Goods of chapters 56 to 62; or":
a good is excluded from heading a heading
    if the heading >= 6301
    and the heading <= 6307
    and the good is described by heading an other heading
    and the other heading >= 6101
    and the other heading <= 6217.

% Note 2(b): worn articles of heading 6309 are not of subchapter I
rule note_63_2b with provenance HTSUS Chapter 63,
        confer "Worn clothing or other worn articles of heading 6309.":
a good is excluded from heading a heading
    if the heading >= 6301
    and the heading <= 6307
    and the good is described by heading 6309.

% Chapter 61 note 2(b) and Chapter 62 note 2(a): worn clothing of 6309 is
% not of Chapters 61 and 62
rule note_61_2b with provenance HTSUS Chapter 61,
        confer "(b) Worn clothing or other worn articles of heading 6309;":
a good is excluded from heading a heading
    if the heading >= 6101
    and the heading <= 6117
    and the good is described by heading 6309.

rule note_62_2a with provenance HTSUS Chapter 62,
        confer "(a) Worn clothing or other worn articles of heading 6309;":
a good is excluded from heading a heading
    if the heading >= 6201
    and the heading <= 6217
    and the good is described by heading 6309.

% Chapter 64 note 1(c): worn footwear is of heading 6309
rule note_64_1c with provenance HTSUS Section XII and Chapter 64, confer "Worn footwear of heading 6309;":
a good is excluded from heading a heading
    if the heading >= 6401
    and the heading <= 6406
    and the good is described by heading 6309.

% Chapter 39 note 2(p): goods of Section XI (here, of Chapter 63) are not of
% Chapter 39
rule note_39_2p with provenance HTSUS Section VII and Chapter 39,
        confer "(p) Goods of section XI (textiles and textile articles);":
a good is excluded from heading a heading
    if the heading >= 3901
    and the heading <= 3926
    and the other heading is in [6301, 6302, 6303, 6304, 6305, 6306, 6307, 6308, 6309, 6310]
    and the good is described by heading the other heading.

% GRI 3(a): heading 6307 is the residual heading of subchapter I ("Other
% made up articles")
rule gri_3a_6307 with provenance HTSUS General Rules of Interpretation,
        confer "The heading which provides the most specific description shall be preferred to headings providing a more general description":
heading a heading is more specific than heading 6307
    if the heading >= 6301
    and the heading <= 6306.

% ---------------------------------------------------------------------------
% The materials the subheadings name, read on what the good is classified
% as consisting of (GRI 3(b)) with Section XI note 2 (section_xi.le).
% ---------------------------------------------------------------------------

jute is a textile bast fibre of heading 5303,
    as stated in HTSUS Chapter 53, confer "Jute and other textile bast fibers (excluding flax, true hemp".
kenaf is a textile bast fibre of heading 5303,
    as stated in HTSUS Chapter 53, confer "Jute and other textile bast fibers (excluding flax, true hemp".

% strip of polyethylene or polypropylene (heading 5404) is a man-made
% textile material of Chapter 54, but not a man-made fibre (Chapter 54
% note 1)
polyethylene strip belongs to man-made fibres,
    as stated in HTSUS Chapter 54, confer "STRIP AND THE LIKE OF MAN-MADE TEXTILE MATERIALS".
polypropylene strip belongs to man-made fibres,
    as stated in HTSUS Chapter 54, confer "STRIP AND THE LIKE OF MAN-MADE TEXTILE MATERIALS".
polyethylene strip is a strip of polyethylene or polypropylene,
    as stated in HTSUS Chapter 63, confer "Other, of polyethylene or polypropylene strip or the".
polypropylene strip is a strip of polyethylene or polypropylene,
    as stated in HTSUS Chapter 63, confer "Other, of polyethylene or polypropylene strip or the".

rule material_cotton with provenance HTSUS Chapter 63, confer "Of cotton (369)":
the chapter sixty-three material of a good is cotton
    if the good is classified as consisting of a component
    and the textile material of the component is cotton.

rule material_wool with provenance HTSUS Chapter 63, confer "of wool or fine animal hair":
the chapter sixty-three material of a good is wool
    if the good is classified as consisting of a component
    and the textile material of the component is wool fibres.

rule material_synthetic with provenance HTSUS Chapter 63, confer "of synthetic fibers":
the chapter sixty-three material of a good is synthetic
    if the good is classified as consisting of a component
    and the textile material of the component is man-made fibres
    and the fibre material of the component is synthetic fibres.

rule material_artificial with provenance HTSUS Chapter 63, confer "Of artificial fibers (666)":
the chapter sixty-three material of a good is artificial
    if the good is classified as consisting of a component
    and the textile material of the component is man-made fibres
    and the fibre material of the component is artificial fibres.

% man-made textile material of strip only: no synthetic or artificial
% fibre in it
rule material_strip with provenance HTSUS Chapter 63,
        confer "Other, of polyethylene or polypropylene strip or the":
the chapter sixty-three material of a good is man-made strip
    if the good is classified as consisting of a component
    and the textile material of the component is man-made fibres
    and the component contains a percentage percent of a material
    and the material is a strip of polyethylene or polypropylene
    and it is not the case that
        the fibre material of the component is a class.

% jute and the other bast fibres of heading 5303: every vegetable fibre of
% the good is one of them, or the one that predominates is
rule material_bast_shares with provenance HTSUS Chapter 63,
        confer "Of jute or of other textile bast fibers of heading 5303":
a good is of bast fibres of heading 5303
    if the good is classified as consisting of a component
    and the textile material of the component is vegetable fibres
    and the component states shares
    and for all cases in which
            the component contains a percentage percent of a material
            and the material belongs to vegetable fibres
        it is the case that
            the material is a textile bast fibre of heading 5303.

rule material_bast_stated with provenance HTSUS Chapter 63,
        confer "Of jute or of other textile bast fibers of heading 5303":
a good is of bast fibres of heading 5303
    if the good is classified as consisting of a component
    and the material that predominates by weight in the component is a material
    and the material is a textile bast fibre of heading 5303
    and it is not the case that
        the component states shares.

rule material_bast with provenance HTSUS Chapter 63,
        confer "Of jute or of other textile bast fibers of heading 5303":
the chapter sixty-three material of a good is bast fibres
    if the good is of bast fibres of heading 5303.

% silk, vegetable fibres other than bast fibres, metalized yarn: "of other
% textile materials"
rule material_other with provenance HTSUS Chapter 63, confer "Of other textile materials":
the chapter sixty-three material of a good is other
    if the good is classified as consisting of a component
    and the textile material of the component is a group
    and it is not the case that
        the group is in [cotton, wool fibres, man-made fibres]
    and it is not the case that
        the good is of bast fibres of heading 5303.

% knitted or crocheted, or not (the fabric of what the good is classified
% as consisting of: section_xi.le)
rule knit_class_knitted with provenance HTSUS Chapter 63, confer "Knitted or crocheted:":
the knit class of a good is knitted
    if the construction of the good is a construction
    and the construction is in [knitted, crocheted].

rule knit_class_other with provenance HTSUS Chapter 63, confer "Not knitted or crocheted, of cotton":
the knit class of a good is other
    if the construction of the good is a construction
    and it is not the case that
        the construction is in [knitted, crocheted].

rule print_class_printed with provenance HTSUS Chapter 63, confer "Other bed linen, printed:":
the print class of a good is printed
    if the good is classified as consisting of a component
    and the fabric of the component is printed.

rule print_class_other with provenance HTSUS Chapter 63, confer "Other bed linen:":
the print class of a good is not printed
    if the good is classified as consisting of a component
    and it is not the case that
        the fabric of the component is printed.

rule towel_fabric_terry with provenance HTSUS Chapter 63,
        confer "Toilet linen and kitchen linen, of terry toweling or similar terry fabrics, of cotton":
the towel fabric of a good is terry
    if the good is classified as consisting of a component
    and the fabric of the component is terry.

rule towel_fabric_other with provenance HTSUS Chapter 63, confer "6302.91.00":
the towel fabric of a good is other
    if the good is classified as consisting of a component
    and it is not the case that
        the fabric of the component is terry.

rule sack_form_fibc with provenance HTSUS Chapter 63, confer "Flexible intermediate bulk containers":
the sack form of a good is fibc
    if the kind of the good is flexible intermediate bulk container.

rule sack_form_other with provenance HTSUS Chapter 63, confer "Other (669)":
the sack form of a good is other
    if the good is described by heading 6305
    and it is not the case that
        the kind of the good is flexible intermediate bulk container.

% Subheading note 1: the bed nets of 6304.20 are of warp knit fabric
% impregnated or coated with one of the insecticides the note names
rule furnishing_bed_net with provenance HTSUS Chapter 63,
        confer "Subheading 6304.20 covers articles made from warp knit fabrics, impregnated or coated with alpha-cypermethrin (ISO)":
a good is a bed net of subheading note one
    if the family of the good is bed net
    and the good is made from warp knit fabric impregnated or coated with an insecticide of subheading note one.

rule furnishing_bed_net_group with provenance HTSUS Chapter 63,
        confer "Bed nets specified in subheading note 1 to this chapter":
the furnishing group of a good is bed net of note one
    if the good is a bed net of subheading note one.

rule furnishing_bedspread with provenance HTSUS Chapter 63, confer "Bedspreads:":
the furnishing group of a good is bedspread
    if the family of the good is bedspread.

rule furnishing_other with provenance HTSUS Chapter 63, confer "Knitted or crocheted":
the furnishing group of a good is other
    if the family of the good is a family
    and the family is in [bed net, furnishing article]
    and it is not the case that
        the good is a bed net of subheading note one.

% ---------------------------------------------------------------------------
% GRI 6: what the subheadings read.
% ---------------------------------------------------------------------------

rule blanket_electric with provenance HTSUS Chapter 63, confer "Electric blankets (666)":
the subheading of a good in heading 6301 is "6301.10"
    if the kind of the good is electric blanket.

rule blanket_subheading with provenance HTSUS General Rules of Interpretation,
        confer "the classification of goods in the subheadings of a heading shall be determined according to the terms of those subheadings and any related subheading notes":
the subheading of a good in heading 6301 is a code
    if it is not the case that
        the kind of the good is electric blanket
    and the chapter sixty-three material of the good is a material
    and the subheading in heading 6301 for the material the material is the code under table blankets.

rule linen_subheading with provenance HTSUS General Rules of Interpretation,
        confer "the classification of goods in the subheadings of a heading shall be determined according to the terms of those subheadings and any related subheading notes":
the subheading of a good in heading 6302 is a code
    if the family of the good is a group
    and the group is in [bed linen, table linen]
    and the knit class of the good is a knit
    and the chapter sixty-three material of the good is a material
    and the print class of the good is a print
    and the subheading in heading 6302 for the group with knit the knit with material the material with print the print is the code under table bed and table linen.

rule toilet_linen_subheading with provenance HTSUS General Rules of Interpretation,
        confer "the classification of goods in the subheadings of a heading shall be determined according to the terms of those subheadings and any related subheading notes":
the subheading of a good in heading 6302 is a code
    if the family of the good is a group
    and the group is in [toilet linen, kitchen linen]
    and the chapter sixty-three material of the good is a material
    and the towel fabric of the good is a fabric
    and the subheading in heading 6302 for the towel material the material with fabric the fabric is the code under table toilet linen.

rule curtain_subheading with provenance HTSUS General Rules of Interpretation,
        confer "the classification of goods in the subheadings of a heading shall be determined according to the terms of those subheadings and any related subheading notes":
the subheading of a good in heading 6303 is a code
    if the knit class of the good is a knit
    and the chapter sixty-three material of the good is a material
    and the subheading in heading 6303 for the knit the knit with curtain material the material is the code under table curtains.

rule bedspread_knitted with provenance HTSUS Chapter 63, confer "Bedspreads: Knitted or crocheted: 6304.11":
the subheading of a good in heading 6304 is "6304.11"
    if the furnishing group of the good is bedspread
    and the knit class of the good is knitted.

rule bedspread_other with provenance HTSUS Chapter 63, confer "Other: 6304.19":
the subheading of a good in heading 6304 is "6304.19"
    if the furnishing group of the good is bedspread
    and the knit class of the good is other.

rule bed_net_subheading with provenance HTSUS Chapter 63, confer "Bed nets specified in subheading note 1 to this chapter":
the subheading of a good in heading 6304 is "6304.20"
    if the furnishing group of the good is bed net of note one.

rule furnishing_subheading with provenance HTSUS General Rules of Interpretation,
        confer "the classification of goods in the subheadings of a heading shall be determined according to the terms of those subheadings and any related subheading notes":
the subheading of a good in heading 6304 is a code
    if the furnishing group of the good is other
    and the knit class of the good is a knit
    and the chapter sixty-three material of the good is a material
    and the subheading in heading 6304 for the furnishing other with knit the knit with material the material is the code under table furnishings.

rule sack_subheading with provenance HTSUS General Rules of Interpretation,
        confer "the classification of goods in the subheadings of a heading shall be determined according to the terms of those subheadings and any related subheading notes":
the subheading of a good in heading 6305 is a code
    if the chapter sixty-three material of the good is a material
    and the sack form of the good is a form
    and the subheading in heading 6305 for the sack material the material with form the form is the code under table sacks.

rule cover_subheading with provenance HTSUS General Rules of Interpretation,
        confer "the classification of goods in the subheadings of a heading shall be determined according to the terms of those subheadings and any related subheading notes":
the subheading of a good in heading 6306 is a code
    if the family of the good is a group
    and the group is in [tarpaulin, tent]
    and the chapter sixty-three material of the good is a material
    and the subheading in heading 6306 for the cover the group of material the material is the code under table tarpaulins and tents.

rule camping_subheading with provenance HTSUS General Rules of Interpretation,
        confer "the classification of goods in the subheadings of a heading shall be determined according to the terms of those subheadings and any related subheading notes":
the subheading of a good in heading 6306 is a code
    if the family of the good is a group
    and the group is in [sail, pneumatic mattress, camping goods]
    and the subheading in heading 6306 for the article the group is the code under table other made up articles.

rule made_up_subheading with provenance HTSUS General Rules of Interpretation,
        confer "the classification of goods in the subheadings of a heading shall be determined according to the terms of those subheadings and any related subheading notes":
the subheading of a good in heading a heading is a code
    if the heading is in [6307, 6308, 6309]
    and the family of the good is a group
    and the subheading in heading the heading for the article the group is the code under table other made up articles.

% an article of 6307 that names no kind, and a worn article of 6309 whose
% family the rules do not read
rule made_up_subheading_no_family with provenance HTSUS General Rules of Interpretation,
        confer "the classification of goods in the subheadings of a heading shall be determined according to the terms of those subheadings and any related subheading notes":
the subheading of a good in heading a heading is a code
    if the heading is in [6307, 6309]
    and the good is described by heading the heading
    and it is not the case that
        the family of the good is a family
    and the subheading in heading the heading for the article none is the code under table other made up articles.

rule rags_sorted with provenance HTSUS Chapter 63, confer "Sorted: 6310.10":
the subheading of a good in heading 6310 is "6310.10"
    if the good is sorted.

rule rags_other with provenance HTSUS Chapter 63, confer "Other: 6310.90":
the subheading of a good in heading 6310 is "6310.90"
    if the family of the good is rag
    and it is not the case that
        the good is sorted.

% ---------------------------------------------------------------------------
% Tests: goods with the facts a reader writes from a ruling.
% ---------------------------------------------------------------------------

query subheading is:
    the subheading of which good is which code.

query heading is:
    the heading of which good is which heading.

query unplaced is:
    which good is not placed by the model.

% Blankets (CBP: the codes the rulings give, at six digits)
